  "body": "`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test probe_tormach` fails 6 of 7 on upstream main (seen while gating #694 after merging upstream/main; that branch touches only Face files):\n\n```\nface_posts_g38_2_and_sets_z_on_the_770mx    FAILED  golden nc/tormach/probe_face.nc is stale\nedge_ / bore_ / corner_ / boss_ ..._on_the_770mx, bore_posts_in_mm_on_a_metric_machine   FAILED (same)\n```\n\n**Cause:** two PRs merged cleanly in text but not in meaning, two minutes apart:\n- #579 (#570, merged 054ecc60) made the probe cycle rapid to the safe plane and *feed* only below it.\n- #583 (#575, merged a24ef551) carried Tormach probe goldens written against the cycle from before #570. Those goldens expect a protected `G38.3` descent from Z1.9685 to the safe plane, where the post now writes `G0 ... Z0.9843` and then the probe move.\n\nThe new output matches #570's intent: no probe rapid runs below the safe plane, which is Z 25 mm = 0.9843 in for these fixtures. So this looks like stale goldens, not a safety regression. The fix should still read each regenerated `.nc` to confirm that, not just accept the diff.\n\n**Done means:** the `probe_tormach` goldens are regenerated on a branch (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`), the diff is read line by line against #570's rule, and the suite passes on main.\n",
